{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1488826-tc-2e-magic-in-aether-and-adventure-\ud83d\ude32","id":1488826,"title":"[TC 2E] Magic in Aether and Adventure! \ud83d\ude32","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-02T08:27:17-07:00","id":1488826,"title":"[TC 2E] Magic in Aether and Adventure! \ud83d\ude32","content":"WE HAVE MAGIC IN TRINITY! \ud83d\ude32 <br /> <br /> P. S. Only I think that Magic is precursor to later Psi energies in later eras? \ud83e\udd14 <br /> <br /> Quoting newest Aether Preview :<br /> 'Scientific Practices<br /> In Aether, there are three major scientific practices: Advanced Science, Aetheric Science, and Mystical Practices.<br /> Advanced Science is the rule of the day. It\u2019s responsible for the many steam-powered contraptions that are now commonplace modern conveyances: trains, steamships, and balloons. Its advances aren\u2019t limited to hardware. Selective breeding of livestock also falls under the purview of Advanced Science.<br /> Aetheric Science is only in its infancy, but already it produces fanciful contraptions once relegated to fiction \u2014 submersibles that explore the mysteries undiscovered beneath the waves and grand dirigibles that ply the skies the same way sailing ships travel the seas. Dread whispers also tell tales of Aether\u2019s ability to even bestow life on dead flesh. The ranks of the scientific elite keep Aetheric Science from the general population. Finally, Mystical Practices are not new to the world but are just beginning to gain acceptance in the halls of academia. They\u2019re responsible such phenomena as tarot decks that foretell the future, channeling the voices of the dead, and even a painting that ages instead of its owner. Practitioners of Advanced and Aetheric Sciences scoff at such things as mere superstition, but none who witness such workings can deny their potency. Anyone\u2019s capable of Advanced Science, but Aetheric Science and Mystical Practices may only be used by Inspired individuals. One must be able to touch the Aether to manipulate it. Advanced Science works as described in the Trinity Continuum Core (p. 90). Aetheric Science and Mystical Practices are both variations on Inspired Science and function the same as the Trinity Continuum Core instructs with their exceptions outlined below.'<br /> <br /> And<br /> ' Mystic Artifacts Mystic Artifacts are those whose principles can be explained by neither steam nor Aether. The only path to understanding them is through Mystical Practices. They create effects beyond the ken of humanity. A Mystic Artifact might be a pair of spectacles that allow the wearer to see beyond the veil and interact with lingering spirits, a tarot deck that shows the subjects whatever source of harm is mostly likely to befall them next, or an amulet that burns red hot in the presence of a lie. Mystic Practices can come from anywhere \u2014 the wisdom passed down in a family from one generation to the next, the traditions of a druid grove or a coven of witches, or the long forgotten magickal lore fiercely guarded by Samuel Liddell MacGregor Mather and the Golden Dawn. They may even be a unique phenomenon manifested by a single individual, unable to be replicated by anyone else. Wherever they come from, the Mystic Artifacts they produce are equal in potency to any Aetheric Contraption. Their workings are only more intangible than those of the material sciences.<br /> Creating Mystic Artifacts Creating Mystic Artifacts largely follows the path laid out in the Trinity Continuum Core for Inspired Science (p. 90), except for a few notable changes. Mystic Artifacts usually produce mental, social, or spiritual effects, the type of things largely impossible for mundane technology to achieve. The flaws a creator unwittingly introduces to them are of a similar vein. They affect the mind, perceptions, and emotions of the bearer. A gentle soul is consumed by murderous rage, or a normally level-headed individual finds his hold on sanity growing increasingly tenuous. Mystic Artifacts don\u2019t require research, experimentation, or the manual labor of assembly. Instead, their creation revolves around meditation, the proper alignment of the heavens, prayers to otherworldly entities, and ritual actions. These Artifacts all require rare, occasionally otherworldly, materials and arcane preparations. These peculiar requirements may result in additional Complications to an Artifact\u2019s creation process. A character\u2019s Paths are vital to any Mystic Artifacts she creates. They\u2019ll inform the approach she takes creating them and their resulting form and function. A traditional witch and an expert in numerology are all capable of creating an Artifact that warns of impending danger, but the way they construct it and thefinal form it takes varies. The witch hails from the Occultist Origin Path. Her early warning Artifact is a set of runes carved from the bones of an animal she sacrificed to the Earth Goddess. Casting the runes tells if a course of action is safe or if it\u2019s likely to result in her physical harm. The numerologist possesses the Academic Role from his career of studying numbers and their hidden meanings. By careful thought and introspection, he creates a mathematical formula through which the numbers surrounding him reveal if a space is safe or not.<br /> The Skills that apply to Aetheric Science rarely apply when creating a Mystic Artifact. Enigmas or Culture are often more appropriate than Science when planning a new Artifact, and Enigmas or Science take the place of Technology when performing the actions. A Mystical Practitioner relies on her mastery over mind and spirit or her investigations into the supernal mysteries to forge Artifacts with power beyond the mere physical. Any attempts to repair or reverse engineer Mystic Artifacts likewise require knowledge from within or expertise in that which lies beyond the mundane. No amount of mastery over biology, chemistry, or physics will allow an inventor to work on an Artifact that operates on a spiritual plane. While a Mystical Practitioner and an Aetheric Scientist find each other\u2019s works impossible, they\u2019re still able to collaborate and create an Artifact or Contraption that synthesizes their expertise. Working together, disciples of both practices can enhance an item from one field to incorporate elements of the other or even invent entirely new devices containing Mystical and Aetheric features. They allow the two creators to operate and maintain their own creation, which makes the contraption nearly impossible to reverse engineer if it\u2019s ever stolen. The thief would need an accomplice with knowledge of the practice he\u2019s ignorant in.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T08:50:50-07:00","id":1488831,"title":"","content":"This isn't new; TC: Adventure also has Artifacts of Enigmatic Power, where Inspired Science can be worked along lines more mystical than scientific. <br /> <br /> That said, TC:\u00c6ther has been dealing with \u201cmagic\u201d from day one, ever since it was revealed that \u00c6ther lets the \u00c6thernaut <i>alter reality according to his will</i>. I even started a thread over in the <b>Mage: the Ascension</b> forum about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-02-2022, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T10:44:51-07:00","id":1488852,"title":"","content":"So from practical point, magician characters are build with particular Paths ( like Occultist or Outsider) and making it Mesmerist by choosing Psychic Gifts? In Aether by making character the Gog or Magog?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T11:04:56-07:00","id":1488856,"title":"","content":"Basically, yes. That said, Adventure! doesn't restrict Artifacts of Enigmatic Power to mesmerists; it just says that the effects tend not to be physical. That <i>tends</i> to exclude stalwarts, at least in theory, as the design concepts for Dynamic Gifts states that they are physical effects; but it's worth noting that the actual list of Dynamic Gifts includes ones based off of mental and social attributes. And besides, Adventure! isn't as strict as \u00c6ther about them <i>having to be</i> non-physical. <br /> <br /> Also, I see no reason to exclude daredevils and Squires. All that's needed is Inspired Science (reskinned as magic by your choice of Path), and that's not forbidden to daredevils and Squires; only Powered Science is forbidden to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T12:11:00-07:00","id":1488863,"title":"","content":"In my home campaign &quot;<a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/Aaronsmonsters?filters&#91;tag]=Heroic%20Age\" target=\"_blank\">The Heroic Age</a>&quot; I focus entirely on Talents, and run with it as far and as weird as I can. I focus strongly on pulpy sci-fi and horror themes, creatures and concepts. And this included magic and supernatural beings.<br /> <br /> Just using Edges, Gifts, Dramatic Editing and Super Science, you can make a wide range of sorcerer, and psychic characters. For wider ranging entities and powers, I have been using Anomalies and custom devices, Edges and such. It is a blast.<br /> <br /> I am particularly looking forward to what is cooked up for Aether. Victorian occultism, vampires, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 08-02-2022, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T16:26:47-07:00","id":1488901,"title":"","content":"Psi has this &quot;magic feeling&quot;, but also does Quantum and Aether (and Flux to certain extend).<br /> Magic is a complex thing to define, you have Force that operates as magic in StarWars, and in the other hand you have all the powers of the BG from Dune that are not magical at all, while can do almost everything force can (except moving things with the mind).<br /> Psi is not different, in Aeon it is completely studied and analized, they have labs and can create technology with it to be used by the general populaton, that is very non-magical. In Adventure! many of the characters see their own powers as magical, and there are a lot of objects that are magical in nature (dont have an scientific explanation to work as they do), yet it is psi (mostly).<br /> Quantum has the same aspect, not understood in Adventure! but explored as something scientific in Aberrant and Aeon.<br /> Honestly, TC, if not for the sci-fi bases, is basically a fantasy setting in the modern/pulp/future/steampunk era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T19:15:11-07:00","id":1488918,"title":"","content":"Trinity might be soft and pulpy sci-fi, but I still prefer it as science fiction where there's no such thing as magic. Personal opinions will vary, but to me anything 'magical' is just stuff the user/witness doesn't understand. Anybody who could tell the future via a tarot deck either has a deck made via the principles of Quantum, Psi, or Flux, or is telling the future themselves and would do it just as well if they were throwing darts at a corkboard or staring into the flames.<br /> <br /> People's opinions will differ from mine, but to me this is what separates Trinity 2e from Chronicles of Darkness. The latter is a grim world of unknown magical where monsters lurk in the shadows to devour us, whereas Trinity is a bright world of Science! where something might be unexplained now, but it eventually will be.<br /> <br /> This is, of course, a separate issue to characters believing their powers to be magic. I suspect that magic in Aether will primarily cover the abilities of those psi and quantum users running around at this point, whereas aetheric science will primarily be based around Flux. But I'm also pretty certain that the categories won't be that neat, and you'll find a bit of everything everywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T19:30:08-07:00","id":1488922,"title":"","content":"Aether has been confirmed not to be Flux, Psi, or Quantum; it's its own thing. <br /> <br /> That said, I tend to agree with your perspective \u2014 although Clarke's Law factors in pretty heavily. We <i>are</i> dealing with a world where the science includes precognition; so it's not terribly surprising that one can make an invention capable of predicting the future. Artifacts of Enigmatic Power simply give it a form that can be thought of as magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T00:19:41-07:00","id":1488946,"title":"","content":"As Doctor Who has played it many times, it can look like magic without being magic. If the rituals are means to adjust the mind to focus energy, which can be tapped by other means, then you're most of the way to the soft fuzzy edge of Sci Fi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T01:35:14-07:00","id":1488950,"title":"","content":"Aether isn\u2019t magic. That doesn\u2019t mean some characters won\u2019t think it is. It\u2019s also the fine distinction in any game that has powers that they\u2019re essentially fitting the same space as magic even though they\u2019re psi, Quantum, Flux, Aether.<br /> <br /> But, no, Aether isn\u2019t magic and the Trinity Continuum continues to be a universe without magic. (Insert usual caveats around sufficiently advanced science, other superpowers, etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 08-03-2022, 04:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T02:30:26-07:00","id":1488958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1488826-tc-2e-magic-in-aether-and-adventure-\ud83d\ude32?p=1488946#post1488946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Doctor Who has played it many times, it can look like magic without being magic. If the rituals are means to adjust the mind to focus energy, which can be tapped by other means, then you're most of the way to the soft fuzzy edge of Sci Fi.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> OR it could look like something else (i.e. Quantum) while being magic.<br /> It's all in the beholder's eye, you know ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27462-william-wilson","name":"William Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T11:31:29-07:00","id":1488995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>William Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1488826-tc-2e-magic-in-aether-and-adventure-\ud83d\ude32?p=1488958#post1488958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> OR it could look like something else (i.e. Quantum) while being magic.<br /> It's all in the beholder's eye, you know ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div>Solid point. I won't argue with such a tight case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T12:09:34-07:00","id":1491018,"title":"","content":"If a stalwart appeared in medieval Europe, he\u2019s clearly going to be called a witch. Whatever people don\u2019t understand could be labeled sorcery. Imagine a parallel-Earth where the Nova Age happens in the Renaissance, a la Marvel\u2019s 1602. Novas might figure out the truth, but, as far as most people are concerned, novas are witches, demons and wizards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T02:48:08-07:00","id":1493395,"title":"","content":"Example Magic Dilemma - I run <b>Adventure</b> story now, inspired by <b>Aether</b> backstory. Our <b><i>Three Prongs</i></b> psiad/mesmerist got vision full of mythological imaginary, seen as coming from <b>Goddess Kali.</b> Is it more or less working with setting as proposed? Truly <i>'fate destiny coming from goddess in your dreams</i>' is possible thing in<b> Trinity</b> now? Talents are run on Flux and luck, in the end?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T11:08:28-07:00","id":1493412,"title":"","content":"Well, it depends on what you mean by \u2018goddess\u2019. A genuine divine being? Probably not. But a nova of incredible power reaching backwards through time? Or a gestalt ascended psionic alien ur-consciousness? Both of those are <i>certainly</i> doable.<br /> <br /> In 1e, novas could travel in time, but it was a power only the very strongest novas could acquire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T11:24:55-07:00","id":1493414,"title":"","content":"Talents lucky is not fate or anything similar, it's them messing with the possibilities unconsciously.<br /> <br /> Its perfectly possible to mess with peoples dreams, you just need Telepathy or some low level Mega Social, not big deal.<br /> <br /> You must understand that the big change in paradigm is not about the powers, the powers are what they are, Psi, Quantum or Flux, the big change in paradigm is the esoteric items. They are equivalent to super science, but instead of using science as a base the explanation of how it works based in other theories, but its still Inspired tech as much as we know. I guess we will see much more about esoteric items in Aegis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T11:36:42-07:00","id":1493415,"title":"","content":"I see the Trinity Continuum as being science-y. Even though PCs and NPCs might <i>believe</i> they\u2019re using magic, but no, it\u2019s actually just science no one yet understands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T12:02:10-07:00","id":1493416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1488826-tc-2e-magic-in-aether-and-adventure-\ud83d\ude32?p=1493412#post1493412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it depends on what you mean by \u2018goddess\u2019. A genuine divine being? Probably not. But a Nova of incredible power reaching backwards through time? Or a gestalt ascended psionic alien ur-consciousness? Both of those are <i>certainly</i> doable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking that if not <b>Fate</b> itself, this vision could grant future <b>Max Mercer</b>, from 200 years or so. But thinking about it - <b>Sara Kaur</b> would be both thematically better suited ( she is Hindu ) and she also is ultrapowerfull Psion/Psiad - that are related to dreams and visions more than other templates. Maybe she deviced some kind transmitter of vision create Psi powers in back in time? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T14:38:55-07:00","id":1493433,"title":"","content":"Remember, for a time, SK Bhurano was possessed by at least one Doyen. It might actually be a Doyen sending the visions!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T02:22:04-08:00","id":1503743,"title":"","content":"How much 'magically' it can get? I'm rewatching <b>Mummy </b>(1999 movie ) and was thinking - <b>Could all the 'sacred rituals' be some kind energy manipulation, reanimating dead?</b> Basiclly, can mummy ( monster ) run on Aether or other energy?<br /> <br /> Also, in <b>Aether </b>era we have direct Dracula and Frankenstein's Monster running on Aether energy, so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T09:39:15-08:00","id":1503758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1488826-tc-2e-magic-in-aether-and-adventure-\ud83d\ude32?p=1503743#post1503743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much 'magically' it can get? I'm rewatching <b>Mummy </b>(1999 movie ) and was thinking - <b>Could all the 'sacred rituals' be some kind energy manipulation, reanimating dead?</b> Basiclly, can mummy ( monster ) run on Aether or other energy?<br /> <br /> Also, in <b>Aether </b>era we have direct Dracula and Frankenstein's Monster running on Aether energy, so...</div> </div> </div> </div>It can go crasily magic to be honest. you can have tarot cards that let you see the future like a clairsentient would, or a tiara that let you read peoples mind for example. They are not super science as we see in Aberrant and Aeon, they are literally powered by the same energies (Psi, Quantum or Flux) but they work on different ways, they just work because they are supposed to. Also, its not Aether, not even aether users could create those items (they probably could replicate the effect, but not the way they work).<br /> <br /> Now, on Dracula, Dracula from Aether is described as over 400 year old, and he was not turned into an vampire, he turned himself into a vampire by alchemy, back when Aether was not named Aether, and when it was not as common as in the Aether era. In other words, Aether eixtis not only during the aether era, it only was particularly common in that period, yet you probably can do aether era science out of aether era.<br /> <br /> There are undead in TC, there are those animated by Electromanipulation, there are those that are animated by quantum power and those animated by aether. Its perfectly possible to say that there are items that can be used to animate dead. The same way as many other exemples os super science, there is mental/procedural super science, for example the Law system of Aeon era China is a supertech system that no normal person can understand, yet it works perfectly balanced based in written laws, and it was created by a Nova before the Aberrant war.<br /> <br /> With all that, its perfectly possible the ritual that created the mummy is actually a super science procedure that animated the body and gave it super powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T13:41:19-08:00","id":1503844,"title":"","content":"Okay, but <b>Imhotep</b> (super)mummy powers? We have Dracula-alchemist that is more or less <b>Castlevania</b> 'my magic is alchemy' vampire. With Psi being able to change physicality of targets, I assume that Psi infused (super)mummy could recreate Imhotep feats? \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K58cPYCTiPM\" data-code=\"K58cPYCTiPM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/K58cPYCTiPM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=omy5TVA-fY0\" data-code=\"omy5TVA-fY0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/omy5TVA-fY0/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-25-2023, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T14:40:57-08:00","id":1503847,"title":"","content":"I would go for Quantum powered Mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T03:39:29-07:00","id":1517259,"title":"","content":"And so we have official 'ghost' in Trinity settings! \ud83d\ude31 #Adventure #Aether<br /> <i>'That\u2019s not to say Carnacki\u2019s solely interested in hoaxers. He\u2019s a fierce foe of the beings who haunt the world of the living, whether they\u2019re lingering impressions left by the dead or entities from beyond the material world. Carnacki prefers identifying and categorizing these manifestations to resolving them; more patient folk find lots of work in cleaning up the fallout from Carnacki\u2019s destructive methods. The notorious \u201cghostfinder\u201d has burned down more than one stately home to rid it of its haunting \u2014 earning numerous enemies in the process.' </i><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/aethernaut-collection-thomas-carnacki/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/aethernaut-collection-thomas-carnacki/\" target=\"_blank\"> [Aethernaut Collection] Thomas Carnacki &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/aethernaut-collection-thomas-carnacki/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://theonyxpath.com/aethernaut-collection-thomas-carnacki/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T18:11:41-07:00","id":1517433,"title":"","content":"Fair enough; I get the sense that, due to Aegis, the TC is more a &quot;sufficiently analyzed magic&quot; setting than hard sci-fi. I like to imagine ghosts as self-reinforcing Dramatic Edit patterns left by people who had Inspiration at the moment of death, or profound emotional feeling. <br /> <br /> They may or may not also be souls, as the Edit might well need a conscious will to observe them into reality, but that is very much in-universe debate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T22:33:13-07:00","id":1517454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1488826-tc-2e-magic-in-aether-and-adventure-\ud83d\ude32?p=1517433#post1517433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough; I get the sense that, due to Aegis, the TC is more a &quot;sufficiently analyzed magic&quot; setting than hard sci-fi. I like to imagine ghosts as self-reinforcing Dramatic Edit patterns left by people who had Inspiration at the moment of death, or profound emotional feeling.<br /> <br /> They may or may not also be souls, as the Edit might well need a conscious will to observe them into reality, but that is very much in-universe debate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Images and sounds from the past can also sometimes manifest near 'weak spots' in time, according to the Player's Guide, even if that weak spot doesn't have a full blown temporal rift. Those kind of echoes of the past feel like one possible explanation for ghostly phenomena in the Trinity Continuum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T06:10:20-07:00","id":1517479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1488826-tc-2e-magic-in-aether-and-adventure-\ud83d\ude32?p=1517454#post1517454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Images and sounds from the past can also sometimes manifest near 'weak spots' in time, according to the Player's Guide, even if that weak spot doesn't have a full blown temporal rift. Those kind of echoes of the past feel like one possible explanation for ghostly phenomena in the Trinity Continuum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Up the thread I invoked <b>Doctor Who </b>, now you're invoking <b>The Stone Tape </b>without saying it. Let's bring <b>Sapphire and Steel</b> and <b>The Children of the Stones</b> into the mix. 1970s British TV was made of this trope. Maybe we need to pull our DVDs out and take copious notes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T22:12:34-07:00","id":1521577,"title":"","content":"I just want to pop in and say I find it silly that in the modern times we disassociate magic with science when the ocultists, wizards and alchemists of the ancient world were also scientists developing thier methodologies and theories. I believe Sir Isac Newtan studied alchemy. This faith based heart non sense came about because of new age stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T12:25:03-07:00","id":1522847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1488826-tc-2e-magic-in-aether-and-adventure-\ud83d\ude32?p=1517433#post1517433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough; I get the sense that, due to Aegis, the TC is more a &quot;sufficiently analyzed magic&quot; setting than hard sci-fi. I like to imagine ghosts as self-reinforcing Dramatic Edit patterns left by people who had Inspiration at the moment of death, or profound emotional feeling.<br /> <br /> They may or may not also be souls, as the Edit might well need a conscious will to observe them into reality, but that is very much in-universe debate.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, we also have various superbeings that can wholly set themselves apart from physicality with Quantum or Psi, like novas with some mad Density Decrease/Phasing or the doyen, who are compose of Psi and plasma. Maybe ghosts in TC are just that stuck on that setting permanently after the death of the physical human body. The requisite Telluric energy might just wash over them due to a stroke of chance or from attraction to the circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T12:42:39-07:00","id":1522851,"title":"","content":"I like to think ghosts are like echoes of people doing things in moments of high flux, possibly they themselves Dramatic editing, but not enough to survive, or events that caused great splits in the multiverse.<br /> As they are echoes they are not capable of evolving or changing their behavior, or maybe even understand they are echoes, but as they are not mere reflections of people, they are partially conscious and react to people around them.<br /> In media Res there is a machine capable of recording people and making them capable of interacting with others, but they are not ghosts, as the real people didn\u2019t die to become those recordings. The Search for the Red Widow has a kind of temple where they summon ghosts from the past, that fight as commanded, they can be copies or echoes, but they are there.<br /> <br /> I think there are a lot of mysteries to be solved in Core and the weird powers of Talents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-28T07:35:20-07:00","id":1523272,"title":"","content":"Of course, there needn't be just one explanation. <br /> <br /> I could see a confluence of Clairvoyance and Telepathy enabling astral projections; and a \u201cPsi ghost\u201d could be an astral projection that survived the death of the body. <br /> <br /> Quantum ghosts would be even more rare, but still possible. Cloak and Phasing can be used to simulate the form of a ghost; and a Nova whose Eruption was triggered by a potentially lethal circumstance could easily believe that she was killed and is now a ghost. For example, Elisa Cameron from Dark Horse Comics' <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghost_(Dark_Horse_Comics)\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost</a> title. There's also <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Negative_Man\" target=\"_blank\">Negative Man</a> from DC's Doom Patrol, and Randy O'Brian from Marvel Comics' New Universe title <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/DP_7\" target=\"_blank\">DP 7</a>, both of whom have the ability to project energy beings to do their bidding: basically immaterial Quantum Agents. And with some minor tweaking, this could be turned into a Quantum version of astral projection as per the Psi ghost from the first paragraph. <br /> <br /> So between those possibilities and the \u201cFlux echoes\u201d described by Mateus Luz, there are plenty of options for ghosts in TC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}